/** @mainpage ZohoInventoryDataProvider Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section zohoinventorydataproviderintro ZohoInventoryDataProvider Introduction

    The %ZohoInventoryDataProvider module provides a data provider API for Zoho Inventory
    through the Zoho Inventory REST API.

    To use this module, use \c "%requires ZohoInventoryDataProvider" in your code.

    All the public symbols in the module are defined in the ZohoInventoryDataProvider namespace.

    The main classes are:
    - @ref ZohoInventoryDataProvider::ZohoInventoryDataProvider "ZohoInventoryDataProvider":
      the root data provider for Zoho Inventory with child providers for contacts, items, orders, etc.

    @par Example:
    @code{.py}
#!/usr/bin/env qore

%requires ZohoInventoryDataProvider
%requires ZohoInventoryRestClient

# Create a REST client with credentials
ZohoInventoryRestClient rest({
    "oauth2_client_id": ENV.ZOHOINVENTORY_CLIENT_ID,
    "oauth2_client_secret": ENV.ZOHOINVENTORY_CLIENT_SECRET,
    "oauth2_refresh_token": ENV.ZOHOINVENTORY_REFRESH_TOKEN,
    "organization_id": ENV.ZOHOINVENTORY_ORGANIZATION_ID,
    "subdomain": "zoho",
    "domain": ".com",
});

# Create a data provider from the REST client
ZohoInventoryDataProvider zoho(rest);

# List items
map printf("Item: %s - %s\n", $1.name, $1.rate),
    zoho.getChildProvider("items").searchRecords();
    @endcode

    @section zohoinventorydataproviderrelnotes Release Notes

    @subsection zohoinventorydataproviderv1_0 ZohoInventoryDataProvider v1.0
    - the initial version of the %ZohoInventoryDataProvider module
*/

#! Contains all public definitions in the ZohoInventoryDataProvider module
public namespace ZohoInventoryDataProvider {
}
